.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH flightlog-restore 1 2026-09-28 "flightlog 0.2.1" "flightlog manual"
.SH NAME
flightlog\-restore \- Put a bundle\*(Aqs session back so its tool can resume it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBflightlog restore\fR [\fB\-\-cwd\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Put a bundle\*(Aqs session back so its tool can resume it.
.PP
Writes the tool\*(Aqs own session files where it looks for them (never overwriting without \-\-force) and prints the command to run: claude \-\-resume, codex resume, opencode import, gemini \-\-resume or cursor\-agent \-\-resume. Paths inside a session are absolute, so resume in a directory holding the same repository.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-cwd\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory to resume in [default: current directory]
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite session files that already exist
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
The .flightlog.zip
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR flightlog (1)
